The rust demo: a virtual Cargo workspace whose crates api and worker depend on pricing, api through [workspace.dependencies] and worker through a path. The change adds a function to pricing and bumps itoa in Cargo.lock. cargo 1.97 wrote Cargo.lock, cargo-nextest 0.9.151 wrote target/nextest/ci/junit.xml and cargo-llvm-cov 0.9.1 wrote lcov.info (cargo llvm-cov nextest --profile ci --workspace --lcov --output-path lcov.info), with the checkout directory rewritten to the GitHub Actions one; the CycloneDX SBOMs are hand-written, with the licences crates.io states.
-- base/.config/nextest.toml --
[profile.ci]
fail-fast = false

[profile.ci.junit]
path = "junit.xml"
-- base/.gitignore --
/target
